# Drop folder for TradingView Pine chart-data exports used by ../tools/compare_tradingview.py.
# Ad-hoc exports are large, local-only scratch — never commit them.
*.csv

# 🔴 EXCEPT golden/ — ONE committed export per engine, so the parity gate can run on EVERY
# clone, on every machine, forever. Before this existed, whether a gate could run at all
# depended on which CSVs happened to be sitting on one laptop: on 2026-09-09 NINE of fourteen
# gates could not answer, so rule 22 ("no engine change without a green gate") was
# unsatisfiable and blocked work instead of gating it.
#
# ⚠ golden is REGRESSION, fresh is ACCEPTANCE, and you need both:
#     golden → catches the PYTHON drifting. Always available, runs in seconds, no human.
#     fresh  → catches PINE and Python disagreeing after a Pine edit. Needs TradingView.
#   A green golden run says NOTHING about a Pine edit made after the file was taken.
!golden/
!golden/*.csv
!golden/*.json
